{
  "id": "ASTIS-RT-20261007-GaussianCompactEntropy",
  "state": "accepted",
  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion-background:gaussian-compact-count-entropy",
    "anchor": "FIRST S4.E6 GaussianLSI background; SLT GaussianPoincare/Limit.lean compact observer and entropy convergence, including L1213-L1234 actual law-to-entropy use; authored literal Bool-count and rootBCF adapter",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.E6",
    "original_text": "ASTIS-authored actual compact-C2 Gaussian/count observer and entropy integration independently sealed before proof.\nFor every real C2 function f with compact support, the actual variance-one centered Gaussian integrates f squared, f squared times log(f squared), and the square of its real derivative. Each actual normalized Bool counting measure integrates those same functions of the signed sum divided by sqrt(N), including N=0. Their positive-index (N+1) count integrals converge respectively to the Gaussian integrals. The corresponding homogeneous entropy, including zero mass, converges to the Gaussian homogeneous entropy. All domains and limits are produced internally.\nExact scope: Authored compact C2 scalar core: same actual allN Bool count/card/signed sqrt-normalized sum and variance-one Gaussian. Three Gaussian L1 plus allN three actual-count L1 domains and successor mass/log-energy/derivative-square/entropy integral limits are produced internally. No supplied law/domain/limit certificate, normalization or positive mass premise. Fullflip-energy factor4, GaussianLSI, finiteHilbert/noncompact actual sqrtRN cutoff, T2/FIRST4.6/main/work/composition remain open.\ntheorem compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits\n    (f : ℝ → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :\n    let μ : (n : ℕ) → Measure (Fin n → Bool) := fun n =>\n      (Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ • Measure.count\n    let S : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Bool) → ℝ := fun n ε =>\n      (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ * ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1\n    let γ : Measure ℝ := gaussianReal 0 1\n    Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2) γ ∧\n    Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) γ ∧\n    Integrable (fun x => (deriv f x)^2) γ ∧\n    (∀ n : ℕ,\n      Integrable (fun ε => (f (S n ε))^2) (μ n) ∧\n      Integrable (fun ε => (f (S n ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S n ε))^2)) (μ n) ∧\n      Integrable (fun ε => (deriv f (S n ε))^2) (μ n)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) atTop\n      (𝓝 (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ∫ ε,\n      (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S (n+1) ε))^2) ∂μ (n+1)) atTop\n      (𝓝 (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ∫ ε, (deriv f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) atTop\n      (𝓝 (∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂γ)) ∧\n    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =>\n      (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S (n+1) ε))^2) ∂μ (n+1)) -\n      (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) *\n        Real.log (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1))) atTop\n      (𝓝 ((∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -\n        (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ)))\n\nIndependent primary/background detail contract:\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"artifact_kind\": \"independent-primary-first-source-API-prerequisite\",\n  \"status\": \"CLOSED_TYPED_OBLIGATION_REFINEMENT\",\n  \"reviewer_id\": \"picard_commit_verifier_20261005\",\n  \"observed_HEAD\": \"6d5df34cdb124e28022f16f566ff549145eb7e65\",\n  \"synthesis_first\": {\n    \"finding\": \"The required compact-C2 entropy/mass/derivative-square convergence needs no new CLT or unbounded-integral theorem. Actual35 output plus three true BCFs and integral-map domain transfer suffices. Use root ofCompactSupport to avoid porting SLT bespoke boundedness/BCF constructors. Zero entropy mass is admitted through continuous tlogt.\",\n    \"smallest_next_target\": \"One genuine actual count-law integration node producing three observer L1 domains on gaussianReal0,1 and every actual finite count law, three observer integral limits and their actual entropy limit, with only f: R->R, ContDiff R 2 f and HasCompactSupport f as public analytic binders. Obtain actual law sequence by calling35 internally; no supplied law/limit/normalizer/L1/entropy certificate.\",\n    \"dependency_ready_condition\": \"35 publicly sealed interface is sufficient, but its exact admitted compiled state is deliberately not certified or inferred by this preread. Mathematical implementation of36 waits35 independent admission.\"\n  },\n  \"primary_first\": {\n    \"source\": {\n      \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-transport-preread/source-primary.raw.snapshot.html\",\n      \"raw_sha256\": \"ec485cdad5fe140114be35eef93d19398e0cafcf21abb3fff1bdbbf462e5f94d\",\n      \"lf_sha256\": \"ec485cdad5fe140114be35eef93d19398e0cafcf21abb3fff1bdbbf462e5f94d\",\n      \"bytes\": 1858750\n    },\n    \"outer_fragments\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"S4.Ex8\",\n        \"UTF8_start\": 277149,\n        \"UTF8_end\": 278916,\n        \"snapshot\": {\n          \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-clt-entropy-preread/primary.S4.Ex8.raw.snapshot.html\",\n          \"raw_sha256\": \"23d12fb9b403c0d49a54342dc2fa78cf6771b89ad9fc94d867f3d3c33d4a02be\",\n          \"lf_sha256\": \"23d12fb9b403c0d49a54342dc2fa78cf6771b89ad9fc94d867f3d3c33d4a02be\",\n          \"bytes\": 1767\n        },\n        \"math_alttext\": [\n          \"\\\\rho_{y}(u)\\\\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\\\\sqrt{\\\\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\\\\sqrt{\\\\eta}\\\\,\\\\langle\\\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\\\\rangle\\\\,.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"S4.SS1.p4.2\",\n        \"UTF8_start\": 278917,\n        \"UTF8_end\": 281134,\n        \"snapshot\": {\n          \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-clt-entropy-preread/primary.S4.SS1.p4.2.raw.snapshot.html\",\n          \"raw_sha256\": \"4c61d3646e7e8c09e3a92ce53b2e01bde97f3469323a440543abe255ecc0a1fd\",\n          \"lf_sha256\": \"4c61d3646e7e8c09e3a92ce53b2e01bde97f3469323a440543abe255ecc0a1fd\",\n          \"bytes\": 2217\n        },\n        \"math_alttext\": [\n          \"0\\\\preceq\\\\nabla^{2}\\\\rho_{y}\\\\preceq\\\\eta I\",\n          \"R_{\\\\eta,y}\",\n          \"(X-x_{y}^{+})/\\\\sqrt{\\\\eta}\",\n          \"u\\\\mapsto e^{-\\\\lVert u\\\\rVert^{2}/2-\\\\rho_{y}(u)}\",\n          \"\\\\mathsf{r}_{y}\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"S4.E6\",\n        \"UTF8_start\": 281135,\n        \"UTF8_end\": 283519,\n        \"snapshot\": {\n          \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-clt-entropy-preread/primary.S4.E6.raw.snapshot.html\",\n          \"raw_sha256\": \"601c07c36f592ec891b13b22cb0574c21a0c6df7e60c7b4fe9d8139c3c9cf822\",\n          \"lf_sha256\": \"601c07c36f592ec891b13b22cb0574c21a0c6df7e60c7b4fe9d8139c3c9cf822\",\n          \"bytes\": 2384\n        },\n        \"math_alttext\": [\n          \"W_{2}(\\\\mathsf{r}_{y},\\\\mathsf{N}(0,I))\\\\leqslant\\\\sqrt{\\\\mathbb{E}_{\\\\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\\\\lVert\\\\nabla\\\\rho_{y}(U)\\\\rVert^{2}]}\\\\leqslant\\\\eta\\\\sqrt{\\\\mathbb{E}_{\\\\mathsf{r}_{y}}\\\\lVert U\\\\rVert^{2}}\\\\leqslant\\\\eta\\\\sqrt{d}\\\\,.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"S4.SS1.p4.3\",\n        \"UTF8_start\": 283520,\n        \"UTF8_end\": 285390,\n        \"snapshot\": {\n          \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-clt-entropy-preread/primary.S4.SS1.p4.3.raw.snapshot.html\",\n          \"raw_sha256\": \"31e5b0a24c6d8b3055713cd2c48ae293a859cc209b5df82150162f4b9a471fa6\",\n          \"lf_sha256\": \"31e5b0a24c6d8b3055713cd2c48ae293a859cc209b5df82150162f4b9a471fa6\",\n          \"bytes\": 1870\n        },\n        \"math_alttext\": [\n          \"\\\\nabla\\\\rho_{y}(0)=0\",\n          \"\\\\nabla\\\\rho_{y}\",\n          \"\\\\eta\",\n          \"\\\\mathsf{r}_{y}\",\n          \"1\",\n          \"0\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"contract\": \"SPHMC S4.E6 first inequality uses full standard-Gaussian LSI AND separate Gaussian Talagrand. It does not print this finite Bernoulli/CLT proof, impose compact support on literal RGO square-root density, or give either dependency for free. This packet is authored compact analytic core only.\"\n  },\n  \"fixed_definitions\": {\n    \"cube\": \"B_N = Fin N -> Bool, actual canonical measurable finite cube.\",\n    \"mu_N\": \"(Fintype.card B_N : ENNReal)^(-1) smul Measure.count; cardinal=2^N>0. Fin0 cube has cardinal1.\",\n    \"S_N\": \"(sqrt(N:Real))^(-1) * sum_i (if eps_i then1 else-1). Exactly same35 output map, no change to +/- convention or scaling. At N0 sum0 and totalized inverse0 give S0=0.\",\n    \"gamma\": \"gaussianReal0 (1:NNReal), exact covariance/variance1.\",\n    \"observables\": {\n      \"A_f\": \"x -> (f x)^2\",\n      \"B_f\": \"x -> (f x)^2 * Real.log((f x)^2)\",\n      \"C_f\": \"x -> (deriv f x)^2\"\n    },\n    \"entropy\": \"Ent_m(f^2) = integral B_f dm - (integral A_f dm)*Real.log(integral A_f dm). No integrability is implicit in totalized integral notation; derive and output the real L1 domains.\"\n  },\n  \"public35_signature_only\": {\n    \"file\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/balanced-rademacher-clt/preproof/signature.prospective.txt\",\n    \"raw_sha256\": \"271595fa838cf28466cf90591d2c6aaa1024b42a1af73d85eee25cfc32e04777\",\n    \"signature_text\": \"theorem balanced_count_sum_tendsto_gaussian :\\n    ∃ laws : ℕ → ProbabilityMeasure ℝ,\\n      (∀ n : ℕ, (laws n : Measure ℝ) =\\n        (((Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ •\\n          (Measure.count : Measure (Fin n → Bool))).map\\n          (fun ε : Fin n → Bool => (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ *\\n            ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1))) ∧\\n      (laws 0 : Measure ℝ) = Measure.dirac 0 ∧\\n      Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => laws (n + 1)) atTop\\n        (𝓝 (⟨gaussianReal 0 1, inferInstance⟩ : ProbabilityMeasure ℝ))\\n\",\n    \"read_scope\": \"Only preproof statement/signature, not production body, blind output, wholemath or source verdict.\"\n  },\n  \"upstream_source\": {\n    \"revision\": \"SLT d0f506f0a695018265dccb33bcb05e2f5ca1c876\",\n    \"license\": \"Apache2 headers in all inspected snapshots; external static references, not compiled local truth.\",\n    \"predicate_expansion\": \"EfronSteinApp.CompactlySupportedSmooth f = ContDiff R 2 f AND HasCompactSupport f; not C-infinity.\",\n    \"actual_parents\": [\n      \"GaussianPoincare.tendsto_integral_f_sq\",\n      \"GaussianPoincare.tendsto_integral_deriv_sq\",\n      \"GaussianPoincare.tendsto_integral_f_sq_mul_log\",\n      \"GaussianPoincare.tendsto_entropy_f_sq\",\n      \"GaussianLSI.gaussian_logSobolev_CompSmo\"\n    ],\n    \"entropy_definition\": \"LogSobolev.entropy exactly same homogeneous real entropy integral, no probability normalization smuggled into f.\",\n    \"split\": \"OneDimGLSICompSmo combines entropy limit and SEPARATE tendsto_sum_sq_shifted_four_deriv_sq. Derivative-square expectation convergence alone is not factor4 full-flip-energy convergence.\",\n    \"direct_placeholder_scan\": [],\n    \"local_compile_status\": \"NOT_PORTED_OR_COMPILED_BY_THIS_PREREAD\"\n  },\n  \"actual_apis\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"MeasureTheory.ProbabilityMeasure.tendsto_iff_forall_integral_tendsto\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/ProbabilityMeasure.lean\",\n      \"line\": 346,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Tendsto probability laws iff all actual real BCF Bochner integrals tend; no test-integral-limit premise in final proposed producer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ofCompactSupport (root namespace)\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Topology/ContinuousMap/BoundedCompactlySupported.lean\",\n      \"line\": 83,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"g : alpha -> gamma, Continuous g, HasCompactSupport g -> alpha ->ᵇ gamma, under NonUnitalNormedRing gamma. Here gamma=R. Its toFun is literally g; empty support included. Root namespace, not BoundedContinuousFunction.ofCompactSupport.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"HasCompactSupport.comp_left\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/Support.lean\",\n      \"line\": 282,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Generated additive theorem of HasCompactMulSupport.comp_left: compact support of f and g(0)=0 -> compact support of g composed with f. No continuity of g needed for this support fact. Use g(t)=t^2 or g(t)=t*log t; both vanish0.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"HasCompactSupport.deriv / tsupport_deriv_subset\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/Support.lean\",\n      \"line\": 60,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Compact derivative support derived from genuine local-zero property, no derivative continuity or C-infinity hypothesis. Continuity separately from C2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ContDiff.continuous_deriv\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/ContDiff/Deriv.lean\",\n      \"line\": 108,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"ContDiff R n f and 1<=n -> Continuous(deriv f). For n=2 actual classical derivative, not arbitrary totalized fderiv representative.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Real.continuous_mul_log / Continuous.mul_log\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Log/NegMulLog.lean\",\n      \"line\": 45,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Entire real t -> t log t is continuous, including t=0 (and negative t); follows actual zero-limit proof. Composition with f^2 works at zeros, no f>0 or mass>0 premise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"MeasureTheory.Continuous.integrable_of_hasCompactSupport\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Function/LocallyIntegrable.lean\",\n      \"line\": 622,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Continuous real observable and genuine compact support imply Integrable for a measure finite on compact sets with Borel/open-measurable topology. A probability measure supplies finite/local-finite/finite-on-compact instances; no final L1 binder needed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"MeasureTheory.integrable_map_measure / Integrable.comp_measurable\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Function/L1Space/Integrable.lean\",\n      \"line\": 356,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"For real observer AEStronglyMeasurable on map and actual measurable S_N, L1(map law) iff L1(observable composed S_N); transfer genuine domains to actual count measure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"MeasureTheory.integral_map_of_stronglyMeasurable / integral_map\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Bochner/Basic.lean\",\n      \"line\": 1032,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Actual map identity gives equal Bochner integrals. The API totalizes nonintegrable integrals; proposed producer must independently output L1 rather than treating equality as evidence of integrability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"MeasureTheory.measurable_of_finite\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/MeasurableSpace/Basic.lean\",\n      \"line\": 291,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Finite domain plus MeasurableSingletonClass -> actual map measurable. True Fin N -> Bool canonical pi sigma algebra satisfies required singleton condition, including N0.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"IsFiniteMeasure.toIsLocallyFiniteMeasure and local-finite/finite-on-compacts instance\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Typeclasses/Finite.lean\",\n      \"line\": 291,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Probability laws have finite mass1; on R this derives locally finite/finite on compacts. Alternate proof can use continuous BCF norm bound plus finite mass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ProbabilityTheory.gaussianReal\",\n      \"file\": \".lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Probability/Distributions/Gaussian/Real.lean\",\n      \"line\": 24,\n      \"actual_contract\": \"Second parameter is variance, not standard deviation. Use exact gaussianReal0,1 from35 signature and ⟨gaussianReal0,1,inferInstance⟩ as ProbabilityMeasure.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"route_at_most_seven_steps\": [\n    \"1. Invoke the actual35 producer internally and destructure laws, everyN exact map identity, N0 dirac0, successor Tendsto to gaussianReal0,1. Freeze this SAME S_N and count normalization; do not replace with generic supplied weak-law premises.\",\n    \"2. Derive continuity and genuine compact support of A_f,B_f,C_f: hf.continuous.pow2; Real.continuous_mul_log.comp; hf.continuous_deriv(1<=2); hs.comp_left with square-zero and tlogt-zero; hs.deriv and square-zero. No additional positivity or regularity premise.\",\n    \"3. Use ROOT ofCompactSupport for each observer to obtain actual real BCFs. Derive their probability-law and gaussian L1 using Continuous.integrable_of_hasCompactSupport (or true bounded finite measure proof). Probability/finite-on-compacts are outputs/typeclass consequences, not premises on f.\",\n    \"4. Apply ProbabilityMeasure.tendsto_iff_forall_integral_tendsto to actual35 Tendsto and each BCF. This produces limits for A_f, B_f and C_f on actual laws(n+1), including signed B_f and zeros.\",\n    \"5. Prove actual S_N measurable via measurable_of_finite for canonical cube, rewrite lawsN via35 exact map, use integrable_map_measure and integral_map with observer actual continuity/strong measurability to output corresponding L1/integral identities under true mu_N. N0 identities remain dirac0, not variance1 approximation.\",\n    \"6. Compose A_f integral convergence with Real.continuous_mul_log.continuousAt.tendsto; subtract from B_f convergence. Entropy limit is valid also when f=0 or integral f²=0; do not divide by mass or assume normalized f.\",\n    \"7. Return same actual finite-law entropy and derivative-square observer limits for Bernoulli LSI consumer. Keep factor4 full-flip-energy MVT/exchangeability limit as a separate next parent, then only combine to compact1D Gaussian LSI after it is independently compiled.\"\n  ],\n  \"local_library_search\": {\n    \"searched\": \"Samplinglib TechnicalLemmas Probability/FunctionalInequalities/Measure for actual entropy limits and bounded law-integral support before suggesting ports. No local actual count-law compact entropy producer found. Existing compact-gradient/L2 DCT and GaussianLipschitzExponential centered-exp DCT are different analytic contracts.\",\n    \"minimal_reuse\": \"Mathlib BCF constructor and weak-integral iff avoid importing any SLT limit implementation. Public34 Bernoulli may supply true mu_N probability/L1 for actual h=f(S_N); public35 supplies true weak law/map. If chosen, both are explicit dependency edges, not new source binders.\",\n    \"what_is_not_claimed\": \"No exhaustive theorem inventory/compiled36/localport or review of current35 implementation.\"\n  },\n  \"typed_first_residual\": {\n    \"class\": \"dependency-ready-actual-integration-adapter\",\n    \"residual\": \"Implement and independently admit actual compact observer construction + allN L1 map/normalization transport and entropy limit against the sealed35 law output. API declarations exist pinned; no compiler/proofsearch conducted here, so elaboration/typeclass details remain untested.\",\n    \"counterexample_to_weak_L1_jump\": \"General weak probability convergence plus individual L1 is insufficient for noncompact unbounded observers: mu_n=(1-1/n)dirac0+(1/n)dirac n tends weakly dirac0, but integral x²=n. Thus actual source noncompact f cannot silently replace compact f at this node.\"\n  },\n  \"source_gap\": [\n    \"This is an authored C_c² core, not full Gaussian LSI on literal noncompact source f=sqrt(dR_y/dgamma).\",\n    \"Cutoff/density extension preserving entropy and Gaussian W1,2 energy, finite-Hilbert/product-domain extension and true Fisher-quarter adapter remain necessary.\",\n    \"Full flip-energy4 limit is independent; derivative observer convergence does not imply it.\",\n    \"Talagrand T2, full first4.6 W2, bias/fullLemma/main/work/composition remain open.\"\n  ],\n  \"cost_boundary\": \"Bounded observer integral convergence gives no transport of arbitrary unbounded algorithm query cost, no numerical runtime/oracle complexity and no TV-to-cost inference.\",\n  \"reuse_earlier_closed_preread\": {\n    \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-clt-entropy-preread/source-detail-packet.json\",\n    \"raw_sha256\": \"158fe4583cc964e6132c19043a11a79197ffc9e14f4a4af8a16762095670835d\",\n    \"scope\": \"Primary anchors/CLT retrieval and explicit separate factor4 route only. No previous source acceptance or decoder used to validate36 proof.\"\n  },\n  \"input_artifacts\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-clt-entropy-preread/source-detail-packet.json\",\n      \"raw_sha256\": \"158fe4583cc964e6132c19043a11a79197ffc9e14f4a4af8a16762095670835d\",\n      \"lf_sha256\": \"158fe4583cc964e6132c19043a11a79197ffc9e14f4a4af8a16762095670835d\",\n      \"bytes\": 16590,\n      \"raw_snapshot\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-compact-entropy-preread/input.000.raw.snapshot\",\n      \"lf_snapshot\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-compact-entropy-preread/input.000.lf.snapshot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-clt-entropy-preread/run.closed.json\",\n      \"raw_sha256\": \"c059230b214df00a353ecb231e2e30a94f3bfbfbe42034fce591e19fe3736e94\",\n      \"lf_sha256\": \"c059230b214df00a353ecb231e2e30a94f3bfbfbe42034fce591e19fe3736e94\",\n      \"bytes\": 26817,\n      \"raw_snapshot\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-compact-entropy-preread/input.001.raw.snapshot\",\n      \"lf_snapshot\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-compact-entropy-preread/input.001.lf.snapshot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-transport-preread/source-primary.raw.snapshot.html\",\n      \"raw_sha256\": \"ec485cdad5fe140114be35eef93d19398e0cafcf21abb3fff1bdbbf462e5f94d\",\n      \"lf_sha256\": \"ec485cdad5fe140114be35eef93d19398e0cafcf21abb3fff1bdbbf462e5f94d\",\n      \"bytes\": 1858750,\n      \"raw_snapshot\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-compact-entropy-preread/input.002.raw.snapshot\",\n      \"lf_snapshot\": \"runs/20261007-companion-priority/gaussian-compact-entropy-preread/input.002.lf.snapshot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\":