    "text": "For every real-valued function f on the real line that is C2 and has compact support, define, for each natural number n (including n = 0), the finite space Omega_n = {epsilon : Fin n -> Bool}, the measure mu_n = (card(Omega_n) : ENNReal)^(-1) times counting measure, and S_n(epsilon) = (sqrt(n : Real))^(-1) times sum over j : Fin n of (1 if epsilon(j) is true, and -1 otherwise). Let gamma = gaussianReal 0 1, the real Gaussian probability measure of mean 0 and variance 1, and let f' denote the real derivative deriv f.\nThe three real functions x -> f(x)^2, x -> f(x)^2 log(f(x)^2), and x -> f'(x)^2 are Bochner integrable against gamma. For every natural n, their compositions with S_n are Bochner integrable against mu_n.\nWrite A_n = integral over Omega_n of f(S_n(epsilon))^2 dmu_n, B_n = integral over Omega_n of f(S_n(epsilon))^2 log(f(S_n(epsilon))^2) dmu_n, and D_n = integral over Omega_n of f'(S_n(epsilon))^2 dmu_n. Write A = integral over Real of f(x)^2 dgamma, B = integral over Real of f(x)^2 log(f(x)^2) dgamma, and D = integral over Real of f'(x)^2 dgamma. As n tends to infinity through the natural numbers, A_(n+1) tends to A, B_(n+1) tends to B, D_(n+1) tends to D, and B_(n+1) - A_(n+1) log(A_(n+1)) tends to B - A log(A), all as scalar convergence in Real.\nThe inverse of zero is zero and the Fin 0 sum is empty, so S_0 = 0 on the singleton space Omega_0; the all-n integrability conclusion includes this case, while the limit sequences use n+1. Real.log is totalized with log(0) = 0, including at zeros of f and at zero mass A_n or A. No positivity, density normalization, integrability certificate, or limit certificate for f is an extra hypothesis.",
